    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "Mouse Back and Forward now use a shared in-plugin browse stack for normal tabs, Data Map, Info, and the embedded GitHub workspace. Windows consumes each X-button press/release sequence before WebView2 can fall through to the chooser URL; one press moves one history entry. The LEXEDITOR wordmark remains the explicit Home control and still shows Save and Exit, Exit Without Saving, or Cancel when the editor is dirty. Hidden Edge completed Back/Forward, dirty Home, main-menu return, service shutdown, and same-window plugin switching. The remaining acceptance check is the physical Back/Forward buttons on your mouse.",
